IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, sections 60 to 64 -- PURCHASE: the
-- title a purchaser acquires, notice of an adverse claim, the warranties given on presenting and on
-- transferring a security, and the right to have a missing endorsement supplied. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. As in cb2-part7-issue.l4: named `<what it works out> within s <section>`; TRUE means
-- the provision applies and has the effect named, FALSE means only that it does not; a rule whose result is
-- a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent. Whether a person is a bona fide purchaser, a broker or a
-- purchaser is worked out by the rules for s 48(2) in cb2-part7-interpretation.l4 and passed here as a plain
-- BOOLEAN: those rules sit in another module, and the inputs they take are the same facts a caller states.
-- Within one module, a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs.

§ `s 60 Title of purchaser`

§§ `s 60(1) Title of purchaser`

-- On delivery the purchaser acquires the rights the transferor had or had authority to convey, except that
-- a purchaser who was a party to fraud or illegality affecting the security, or who as a prior holder had
-- notice of an adverse claim, does not improve their position by taking from a later bona fide purchaser.
-- NOTHING: there was no delivery, so s 60(1) says nothing.
-- src:901 | Purchase
-- src:902 | Title of purchaser
-- src:903 | 60 (1) On delivery of a security the purchaser acquires the rights in the security that the transferor had or had authority to convey, except that a purchaser who has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security or who as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim does not improve their position by taking from a later bona fide purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 60(1) (src:901-903)
DECLARE `Rights a purchaser acquires on delivery under s 60(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the purchaser acquires the rights the transferor had or had authority to convey`
    `the purchaser does not improve their position by taking from a later bona fide purchaser`

-- src:901 | Purchase
-- src:902 | Title of purchaser
-- src:903 | 60 (1) On delivery of a security the purchaser acquires the rights in the security that the transferor had or had authority to convey, except that a purchaser who has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security or who as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim does not improve their position by taking from a later bona fide purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 60(1) (src:901-903)
GIVEN `the security is delivered to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser takes from a later bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Rights a purchaser acquires on delivery under s 60(1)`
`the rights the purchaser acquires on delivery within s 60(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the security is delivered to the purchaser`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     (   `the purchaser has been a party to any fraud or illegality affecting the security`
                 OR `the purchaser as a prior holder had notice of an adverse claim`)
            AND `the purchaser takes from a later bona fide purchaser`
         THEN JUST `the purchaser does not improve their position by taking from a later bona fide purchaser`
         ELSE JUST `the purchaser acquires the rights the transferor had or had authority to convey`

§§ `s 60(2) Title of bona fide purchaser`

-- src:904 | Title of bona fide purchaser
-- src:905 | (2) A bona fide purchaser, in addition to acquiring the rights of a purchaser, also acquires the security free from any adverse claim.
@ref CBCA s 60(2) (src:904-905)
GIVEN `the security is delivered to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the bona fide purchaser acquires the security free from any adverse claim within s 60(2)` MEANS
        `the security is delivered to the purchaser`
    AND `the purchaser is a bona fide purchaser`

§§ `s 60(3) Limitation of the purchase`

-- "Only to the extent of the interest or right purchased": the extent is a quantity (a number of
-- securities, or a fraction of the right) and the right the purchaser claims must not exceed it.
-- src:906 | Limitation of the purchase
-- src:907 | (3) A purchaser acquires rights only to the extent of the interest or right purchased.
@ref CBCA s 60(3) (src:906-907)
GIVEN `the extent of the interest or right purchased` IS A NUMBER
      `the extent of the interest or right the purchaser claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser acquires the right claimed within s 60(3)` MEANS
    `the extent of the interest or right the purchaser claims` AT MOST `the extent of the interest or right purchased`

§ `s 61 Deemed notice of adverse claim`

§§ `s 61(1) Deemed notice of adverse claim`

-- A purchaser, or any broker for a seller or purchaser, is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim if (a)
-- the security, in bearer or registered form, has been endorsed "for collection" or "for surrender" or for
-- another purpose not involving transfer; or (b) the security is in bearer form and has on it a statement
-- that it is the property of a person other than the transferor (the mere writing of a name is not one).
-- src:908 | Deemed notice of adverse claim
-- src:909 | 61 (1) A purchaser of a security, or any broker for a seller or purchaser, is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim if
-- src:910 | (a) the security, whether in bearer or registered form, has been endorsed “for collection” or “for surrender” or for some other purpose not involving transfer; or
-- src:911 | (b) the security is in bearer form and has on it a statement that it is the property of a person other than the transferor, except that the mere writing of a name on a security is not such a statement.
@ref CBCA s 61(1) (src:908-911)
GIVEN `the security has been endorsed "for collection" or "for surrender" or for some other purpose not involving transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security has on it a statement that it is the property of a person other than the transferor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is the mere writing of a name on the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser or broker is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim within s 61(1)` MEANS
        `the security has been endorsed "for collection" or "for surrender" or for some other purpose not involving transfer`
    OR  (    `the security is in bearer form`
         AND `the security has on it a statement that it is the property of a person other than the transferor`
         AND (NOT `the statement is the mere writing of a name on the security`))

§§ `s 61(2) Notice of fiduciary duty`

-- A purchaser or broker who has notice that a security is held for a third person, or is registered in the
-- name of or endorsed by a fiduciary, has no duty to inquire into the rightfulness of the transfer and no
-- notice of an adverse claim, except where they know that the consideration is to be used for, or that the
-- transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary's
-- duty: then they are deemed to have notice of an adverse claim.
-- src:912 | Notice of fiduciary duty
-- src:913 | (2) Notwithstanding that a purchaser, or any broker for a seller or purchaser, has notice that a security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary, they have no duty to inquire into the rightfulness of the transfer and have no notice of an adverse claim, except that where they know that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary’s duty, the purchaser or broker is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim.
@ref CBCA s 61(2) (src:912-913)
GIVEN `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser or broker knows that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary's duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the purchaser or broker is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim within s 61(2)` MEANS
    IF `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary`
    THEN JUST `the purchaser or broker knows that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary's duty`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:912 | Notice of fiduciary duty
-- src:913 | (2) Notwithstanding that a purchaser, or any broker for a seller or purchaser, has notice that a security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary, they have no duty to inquire into the rightfulness of the transfer and have no notice of an adverse claim, except that where they know that the consideration is to be used for, or that the transaction is for, the personal benefit of the fiduciary or is otherwise in breach of the fiduciary’s duty, the purchaser or broker is deemed to have notice of an adverse claim.
@ref CBCA s 61(2) (src:912-913)
GIVEN `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the purchaser or broker has a duty to inquire into the rightfulness of the transfer within s 61(2)` MEANS
    IF `the purchaser or broker has notice that the security is held for a third person or is registered in the name of or endorsed by a fiduciary`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 62 Staleness as notice of adverse claim`

-- An event that creates a right to immediate performance of the principal obligation, or sets a date for
-- presentation or surrender, is not of itself notice of an adverse claim, except in a purchase (a) after one
-- year from any date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange, or (b) after six months
-- from any date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender, if funds are available for
-- payment on that date. TRUE when the event is of itself notice; NOTHING for a date means none was set.
-- src:914 | Staleness as notice of adverse claim
-- src:915 | 62 An event that creates a right to immediate performance of the principal obligation evidenced by a security or that sets a date on or after which the security is to be presented or surrendered for redemption or exchange is not of itself notice of an adverse claim, except in the case of a purchase
-- src:916 | (a) after one year from any date set for such presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange; or
-- src:917 | (b) after six months from any date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender of the security if funds are available for payment on that date.
@ref CBCA s 62 (src:914-917)
GIVEN `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `funds are available for payment on the date set for payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the purchase` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the event is of itself notice of an adverse claim within s 62` MEANS
        (    CONSIDER `the date set for presentation or surrender for redemption or exchange`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST d THEN `the date of the purchase` GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 1, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` d))
    OR  (    `funds are available for payment on the date set for payment`
         AND CONSIDER `the date set for payment of money against presentation or surrender`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST d THEN `the date of the purchase` GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `counted from` d))

§ `s 63 Warranties`

§§ `s 63(1) Warranties to issuer`

-- src:918 | Warranties to issuer
-- src:919 | 63 (1) A person who presents a security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange warrants to the issuer that the person is entitled to the registration, payment or exchange, except that a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer warrants only that the purchaser has no knowledge of any unauthorized signature in a necessary endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 63(1) (src:918-919)
DECLARE `Warranty given under s 63` IS ONE OF
    `a warranty to the issuer that the person is entitled to the registration, payment or exchange`
    `a warranty to the issuer that the purchaser has no knowledge of any unauthorized signature in a necessary endorsement`
    `a warranty to the purchaser that the transfer is effective and rightful`
    `a warranty to the purchaser that the security is genuine and has not been materially altered`
    `a warranty to the purchaser that the transferor knows of nothing that might impair the validity of the security`
    `a warranty by an intermediary of their good faith`
    `a warranty by an intermediary of their authority`

-- The person who presents a security for registration of transfer, payment or exchange warrants to the
-- issuer that they are entitled to it, except that a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim
-- who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer warrants only that
-- they have no knowledge of any unauthorized signature in a necessary endorsement.
-- src:918 | Warranties to issuer
-- src:919 | 63 (1) A person who presents a security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange warrants to the issuer that the person is entitled to the registration, payment or exchange, except that a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer warrants only that the purchaser has no knowledge of any unauthorized signature in a necessary endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 63(1) (src:918-919)
GIVEN `the person presents the security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
`the warranties given to the issuer within s 63(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person presents the security for registration of transfer or for payment or exchange`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who receives a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer`
         THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty to the issuer that the purchaser has no knowledge of any unauthorized signature in a necessary endorsement`)
         ELSE JUST (LIST `a warranty to the issuer that the person is entitled to the registration, payment or exchange`)

§§ `s 63(2) Warranties to purchaser`

-- src:920 | Warranties to purchaser
-- src:921 | (2) A person by transferring a security to a purchaser for value warrants only that
-- src:922 | (a) the transfer is effective and rightful;
-- src:923 | (b) the security is genuine and has not been materially altered; and
-- src:924 | (c) the person knows of nothing that might impair the validity of the security.
@ref CBCA s 63(2) (src:920-924)
GIVEN `the person transfers the security to a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
`the warranties given to the purchaser within s 63(2)` MEANS
    IF `the person transfers the security to a purchaser for value`
    THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty to the purchaser that the transfer is effective and rightful`,
                    `a warranty to the purchaser that the security is genuine and has not been materially altered`,
                    `a warranty to the purchaser that the transferor knows of nothing that might impair the validity of the security`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 63(3) Warranties of intermediary`

-- src:925 | Warranties of intermediary
-- src:926 | (3) Where a security is delivered by an intermediary known by the purchaser to be entrusted with delivery of the security on behalf of another or with collection of a draft or other claim to be collected against such delivery, the intermediary by such delivery warrants only the intermediary’s good faith and authority even if the intermediary has purchased or made advances against the draft or other claim to be collected against the delivery.
@ref CBCA s 63(3) (src:925-926)
GIVEN `the security is delivered by an intermediary known by the purchaser to be entrusted with delivery on behalf of another or with collection of a draft or other claim against the delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
`the warranties given by the intermediary within s 63(3)` MEANS
    IF `the security is delivered by an intermediary known by the purchaser to be entrusted with delivery on behalf of another or with collection of a draft or other claim against the delivery`
    THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty by an intermediary of their good faith`, `a warranty by an intermediary of their authority`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 63(4) Warranties of pledgee`

-- A pledgee or other holder for security who redelivers a security received, or after payment and on the
-- debtor's order delivers it to a third person, gives only the warranties of an intermediary.
-- src:927 | Warranties of pledgee
-- src:928 | (4) A pledgee or other holder for purposes of security who redelivers a security received, or after payment and on order of the debtor delivers that security to a third person, gives only the warranties of an intermediary under subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 63(4) (src:927-928)
GIVEN `the person is a pledgee or other holder for purposes of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person redelivers a security received, or after payment and on the order of the debtor delivers it to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given under s 63`)
`the warranties given by the pledgee within s 63(4)` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a pledgee or other holder for purposes of security`
       AND `the person redelivers a security received, or after payment and on the order of the debtor delivers it to a third person`
    THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty by an intermediary of their good faith`, `a warranty by an intermediary of their authority`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 63(5) Warranties of broker`

-- src:929 | Warranties of broker
-- src:930 | (5) A broker gives to a customer, to the issuer or to a purchaser, as the case may be, the warranties provided in this section and has the rights and privileges of a purchaser under this section, and those warranties of and in favour of the broker acting as an agent or mandatary are in addition to warranties given by the customer and warranties given in favour of the customer.
@ref CBCA s 63(5) (src:929-930)
GIVEN `the person is a broker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the broker gives the warranties and has the rights and privileges of a purchaser under this section within s 63(5)` MEANS
    `the person is a broker`

-- src:929 | Warranties of broker
-- src:930 | (5) A broker gives to a customer, to the issuer or to a purchaser, as the case may be, the warranties provided in this section and has the rights and privileges of a purchaser under this section, and those warranties of and in favour of the broker acting as an agent or mandatary are in addition to warranties given by the customer and warranties given in favour of the customer.
@ref CBCA s 63(5) (src:929-930)
GIVEN `the person is a broker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the broker acts as an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the broker's warranties are in addition to those given by and in favour of the customer within s 63(5)` MEANS
        `the person is a broker`
    AND `the broker acts as an agent or mandatary`

§ `s 64 Right to compel endorsement`

-- When a security in registered form is delivered to a purchaser without a necessary endorsement, the
-- purchaser may become a bona fide purchaser only as of the time the endorsement is supplied; but against the
-- transferor the transfer is complete on delivery and the purchaser has a specifically enforceable right to
-- have the endorsement supplied. NOTHING: the security is not in registered form, or it was delivered with
-- its necessary endorsement, so s 64 says nothing.
-- src:931 | Right to compel endorsement
-- src:932 | 64 When a security in registered form is delivered to a purchaser without a necessary endorsement, the purchaser may become a bona fide purchaser only as of the time the endorsement is supplied, but against the transferor the transfer is complete on delivery and the purchaser has a specifically enforceable right to have any necessary endorsement supplied.
@ref CBCA s 64 (src:931-932)
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the endorsement has been supplied by the time asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the purchaser may be a bona fide purchaser at the time asked about within s 64` MEANS
    IF     `the security is in registered form`
       AND `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement`
    THEN JUST `the endorsement has been supplied by the time asked about`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:931 | Right to compel endorsement
-- src:932 | 64 When a security in registered form is delivered to a purchaser without a necessary endorsement, the purchaser may become a bona fide purchaser only as of the time the endorsement is supplied, but against the transferor the transfer is complete on delivery and the purchaser has a specifically enforceable right to have any necessary endorsement supplied.
@ref CBCA s 64 (src:931-932)
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`against the transferor the transfer is complete on delivery and the purchaser may enforce the supplying of the endorsement within s 64` MEANS
        `the security is in registered form`
    AND `the security is delivered to the purchaser without a necessary endorsement`
